Now I have the test code and the formal catalog loaded. Let me apply the **testsmells.org 19-smell academic taxonomy** with integration-test calibration.

---

## Test Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest v4 · **.NET 10** · **Integration tests** (class has `[TestCategory("Integration")]`)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 2 | 2 |
| Medium | 1 | 1 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **3** | **3** |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Smell 4: Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Location:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Problem:** No assertion. This test passes even if `Insert` silently drops every record. Being an integration test doesn't excuse missing verification — we still must confirm the side-effect.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Smell 1: Conditional Test Logic

**Location:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** The `if/else` means only one branch ever executes per run. The test silently skips the other path, hiding a gap. You don't know which assertion actually fires.

**Fix:** Write two focused tests with deterministic arrange:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsNameCorrectly()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "VIP", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;

    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Smell 3: Sleepy Test (calibrated down from High)

**Location:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Problem:** 3-second wall-clock sleep makes the suite slow and timing-dependent. However, because this is a `[TestCategory("Integration")]` test that appears to be testing an actual async notification pipeline, severity is **downgraded from High to Medium**.

**Fix:** Replace with a polling/retry helper with a timeout:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}

private static async Task<bool> WaitUntilAsync(Func<bool> condition, TimeSpan timeout)
{
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow + timeout;
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (condition()) return true;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
    return false;
}
```

